  "text": "Hi Northwind Outdoor Support, I’m reaching out regarding my recent account closure. I run a small outdoor gear rental business, and I’m currently in the middle of a year-end audit. I understand that standard account deletion requests have a 30-day cooling-off period before data is purged, but I’m hoping you might be able to expedite this process for me. My accountant needs to verify that all transaction records are fully removed from your active systems to ensure compliance with our internal data privacy protocols. I know this is a bit of an ask, especially since I understand that financial records are retained for 7 years even after account deletion for legal and tax purposes. However, I’m specifically concerned about the active customer profile data and order history that might still be accessible during that 30-day window. Is there any way to shorten that waiting period or confirm that the purge happens immediately upon request? I’d really appreciate any flexibility you can offer to help me close out this fiscal year cleanly. Thanks so much for your help."
